{
 "result": "maze.py is a flat-bytearray BFS: it pads the grid with a '#' border, finds S and E, marks visited cells by overwriting them with '#', expands the frontier level by level, and prints the step count at E or -1. It passes all three public samples (2008, -1, 78) and runs in about 0.02 s on the 40x40 samples and 0.17 s on the 1000x1000 one. The assay was accepted with baseline median 3.52032 and noise 6.9%. I am resting rather than spending the remaining 23 energy on variants, since further gains would likely be within noise and the body is already sound.",
